      "rationale": "This is the terminating base equation for the named outputOK proof predicate: once the current index is past N, an empty remaining sequence satisfies the summary.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-55fa05d4b7990a68e203e8b15296e11489577bd53e5c352747785f464ae79cf1",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule outputOK(.ValSeq, I:Int, N:Int, _F:Int, _T:Int) => true\n    requires I >Int N"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "db034c4631f6721f201f955ef113ee2a18fe8458a2e631d046dc5323df2d45ce",
      "rationale": "This is the even-index recurrence defining outputOK: it consumes the factorial-valued head and advances both accumulators and the index.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-db034c4631f6721f201f955ef113ee2a18fe8458a2e631d046dc5323df2d45ce",
      "start_line": 12,
      "text": "  rule outputOK(vCons(V:Int, REST:ValSeq),\n                I:Int, N:Int, F:Int, T:Int)\n    => outputOK(REST, I +Int 1, N, F *Int I, T +Int I)\n    requires I <=Int N andBool pyMod(I, 2) ==Int 0\n      andBool V ==Int F *Int I"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 21,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "7f063b6288ed1ca9af618a843891c9fb41fc39c7ea5c85c2cba58238be877bf7",
      "rationale": "This is the odd-index recurrence defining outputOK: it consumes the triangular-sum-valued head and advances both accumulators and the index.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7f063b6288ed1ca9af618a843891c9fb41fc39c7ea5c85c2cba58238be877bf7",
      "start_line": 17,
      "text": "  rule outputOK(vCons(V:Int, REST:ValSeq),\n                I:Int, N:Int, F:Int, T:Int)\n    => outputOK(REST, I +Int 1, N, F *Int I, T +Int I)\n    requires I <=Int N andBool notBool (pyMod(I, 2) ==Int 0)\n      andBool V ==Int T +Int I"
    }
  ],
