      "rationale": "This simplification adds associativity of ValSeq concatenation, an algebraic fact about the pre-existing valSeqConcat operation that is assumed by the verification module and is not separately proved in Stage 1.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-9345c98e84d84ccfaeba7d804fe62d2d3a9744b1ef482585fa67ea3fb0a09b97",
      "start_line": 25,
      "text": "  rule valSeqConcat(valSeqConcat(A:ValSeq, B:ValSeq), C:ValSeq)\n    => valSeqConcat(A, valSeqConcat(B, C))\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DOMAIN_LEMMA",
      "discovery_manifest_sha256": "cd5a215d73f441e91cef5b00ac023703e39d736318f40555997847e520f4aeb1",
      "end_line": 29,
      "inventory_sha256": "a51d8b2c346e72b06c592a426e9e98ee5acf2554dd48cf0c23e835041070ae4e",
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "1bc30aceb4ec6e423c8f79079ea7b1c195de5d88396229aa8ee74794085384fa",
      "rationale": "This simplification adds the right-identity law for the pre-existing valSeqConcat operation; the reference definition only computes structurally from the left, and Stage 1 supplies this additional algebraic fact without a prior exact proof.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-1bc30aceb4ec6e423c8f79079ea7b1c195de5d88396229aa8ee74794085384fa",
      "start_line": 28,
      "text": "  rule valSeqConcat(A:ValSeq, .ValSeq) => A\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DOMAIN_LEMMA",
      "discovery_manifest_sha256": "cd5a215d73f441e91cef5b00ac023703e39d736318f40555997847e520f4aeb1",
      "end_line": 35,
      "inventory_sha256": "a51d8b2c346e72b06c592a426e9e98ee5acf2554dd48cf0c23e835041070ae4e",
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "4bb6de9678be64ad9a5dbb1d96a9acd747002bd379e02e9adb311bd159bf6396",
      "rationale": "This simplification assumes left cancellation of a common ValSeq prefix under equality, an additional mathematical property used to expose the existential suffix and not an operational rule or separately proved Stage 1 theorem.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-4bb6de9678be64ad9a5dbb1d96a9acd747002bd379e02e9adb311bd159bf6396",
      "start_line": 32,
      "text": "  rule { valSeqConcat(P:ValSeq, A:ValSeq)\n         #Equals valSeqConcat(P, B:ValSeq) }\n    => { A #Equals B }\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
